a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-e2bf30c6-7292-47b6-96b1-1bb9a4ff7feb-attributes-textdecoration:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-e2bf30c6-7292-47b6-96b1-1bb9a4ff7feb-attributes-textalign:center;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-e2bf30c6-7292-47b6-96b1-1bb9a4ff7feb-attributes-fontfamily:Quicksand;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-e2bf30c6-7292-47b6-96b1-1bb9a4ff7feb-attributes-fontweight:400;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-e2bf30c6-7292-47b6-96b1-1bb9a4ff7feb-attributes-lineheight:125%;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-e2bf30c6-7292-47b6-96b1-1bb9a4ff7feb-attributes-textshadow:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-e2bf30c6-7292-47b6-96b1-1bb9a4ff7feb-attributes-textstroke:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-e2bf30c6-7292-47b6-96b1-1bb9a4ff7feb-attributes-letterspacing:0px;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-e2bf30c6-7292-47b6-96b1-1bb9a4ff7feb-attributes-texttransform:undefined"><span style="width:100%"><p>Painkillers only target the second trigger behind period pain. That’s why they don’t always provide full relief for intense cramps —and for some, they don’t work at all.*<br><br><br>Yet, many women find themselves taking more than they’d like just to get through their period, despite the fact that even light use is known to cause gut and gastrointestinal issues.*<br><br><br>The problem? Painkillers can't fix your hormones, and they definitely don’t fill nutrient gaps. That’s why the pain keeps coming back just as strong every month — along with the bloating, fatigue, and mood swings that make periods even harder.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><br><strong><u>But here's the good news:<br></u></strong><br><br>Leading specialists in menstrual health have found that by tackling all three underlying triggers at once, you can get ahead of cramps before they start — becoming the woman who barely notices them and doesn’t have to battle PMS or other monthly symptoms— thanks to a breakthrough approach.</p></span></div><div data-rid="5f44f034-bc4d-451c-8175-4534bd96acdf" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" tabindex="0" role="link" class="r-15uzt8p alchemy-rte" style="--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-color:#2A2A2A;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-fontsize:12px;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-textdecoration:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-fontfamily:Quicksand;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-fontweight:700;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-lineheight:16px;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-textshadow:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-textstroke:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-letterspacing:0px;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-texttransform:undefined"><span style="width:100%"><p>For references and/or sources, click <u>here</u></p></span></div></div></div><div data-replo-marquee-root="true" data-rid="5519c229-dac7-4d76-a608-1e7f9d7080ce" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0" class="r-1yx501g"><div class="r-1nmrijo" data-replo-marquee-track="true"><div data-rid="aee80130-0347-4151-a306-de9ae03aeb71" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" clas